Feature:

Background: This executes once per feature file
	Given these properties
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|testray.main.component.name|Invite Members|

Setup: This executes before each scenario 
	Given TestCase set Up Portal Instance
	When User first Login PG
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User add CP
		|userEmailAddress|userea@liferay.com|
		|userFirstName|userfn|
		|userLastName|userln|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	Then User edit Password CP
		|password|password|
		|userEmailAddress|userea@liferay.com|
		|userScreenName|usersn|

Teardown: This executes after each scenario 
	Given PortalInstances tear Down CP
		|testPortalInstance|TestPropsUtil#get('test.portal.instance')|
Scenario: View New Site Member
Priority: 4
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	When Site add Blank CP
		|siteName|Site Name|
	And Page add
		|pageName|Site Page 1|
	And Navigator goto Site Page
		|pageName|Site Page 1|
		|siteName|Site Name|
	And Portlet add PG
		|portletName|Invite Members|
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Members
		|portlet|Site Memberships|
	And AssertElementNotPresent the value 'usersn' at locator 'Card#SPECIFIC_TEXT'
	And Navigator goto Site Page
		|pageName|Site Page 1|
		|siteName|Site Name|
	And InviteMembers invite Members
		|inviteUserFullName|userfn userln|
	And User logout PG
	And User login User PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|userea@liferay.com|
	And Notifications view Badge Count
		|notificationCount|1|
	And Notifications goto Notifications
	And Notifications view Request
		|requestsTitle|Test Test invited you to join Site Name.|
	And Notifications accept Request
		|requestsTitle|Test Test invited you to join Site Name.|
	And Refresh
	And Notifications view No Request
	And User logout PG
	And User login User PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@liferay.com|
	And Navigator goto Site Page
		|pageName|Site Page 1|
		|siteName|Site Name|
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Members
		|portlet|Site Memberships|
	Then Site view Member CP
		|userFirstName|userfn|
		|userLastName|userln|
		|userScreenName|usersn|